T have this exact top-level shape:\n   {\n     \"native\": \"<obsolete_assertion|implementation_defect>\",\n     \"external\": \"<obsolete_assertion|implementation_defect>\",\n     \"evidence\": { ... }\n   }\n   - \"native\" and \"external\" are TOP-LEVEL string values, exactly one of the two allowed strings each.\n   - \"evidence\" is a SEPARATE nested object holding your supporting detail (e.g. per-case: what requirements.md says, what the test asserted, what the code returned, what you changed). Structure inside \"evidence\" is your call, but keep it factual and specific.\n   - Validate it parses: python3 -m json.tool diagnosis.json (preauthorized).\n4. If you notice unrelated improvement ideas (code quality, test structure, repo hygiene), write them to improvements.md in the project root. Do NOT implement them. If you have none, do not create the file.\n\nHARD CONSTRAINTS\n- Implementation changes are limited to lifecycle.py and test_lifecycle.py. New files diagnosis.json and improvements.md are expected and allowed.\n- Do NOT modify requirements.md or backlog.md, or any other existing file.\n- Do NOT delete any file. Do NOT add dependencies (stdlib only). Do NOT publish anything, do not create artifacts, do not commit or push.\n- Do not act on the pending CEO decision D-7 (transcription provider) \u2014 it is a separate project and out of scope.\n\nREPORT BACK\n- The two classifications and the one-line reason for each.\n- Exact diffs you made (file, before, after).\n- Verbatim test output.\n- The final contents of diagnosis.json and improvements.md (if written)."}, "is_error": true, "tool_denial_kind": "permission-rule", "timestamp": "2026-09-09T14:47:15.379Z", "result": "PreToolUse:Agent hook error: [python3 /var/folders/mx/w46p9btx1t17wv9tbsq885qw0000gn/T/richos-owned-wake-native-mmdlv6q8/adapter-hook-log.py python3 /private/var/folders/mx/w46p9btx1t17wv9tbsq885qw0000gn/T/richos-owned-wake-native-mmdlv6q8/runtime-snapshot/engine/scripts/lib/owned-dispatch.p