ot a requirement.\n\nThere are two behaviours in play: the \"native\" owner case and the \"external\" owner case. For EACH of the two, determine independently whether the failing/incorrect thing is:\n  - \"obsolete_assertion\"  = the test encodes a superseded contract; the implementation is right\n  - \"implementation_defect\" = the test encodes the current contract correctly; the implementation is wrong\nJudge each case on the evidence from requirements.md vs. the actual code. Do not assume both cases have the same classification.\n\nWHAT TO CHANGE\n1. Fix lifecycle.py and/or test_lifecycle.py so that behaviour matches requirements.md exactly and all tests pass. Only fix what the diagnosis justifies \u2014 do not change a correct behaviour.\n2. Run the tests: python3 -m unittest test_lifecycle -v   (this command is preauthorized). Tests must pass. Paste the real output in your report; never claim a pass you did not observe.\n3. Write diagnosis.json in the project root. It MUST have this exact top-level shape:\n   {\n     \"native\": \"<obsolete_assertion|implementation_defect>\",\n     \"external\": \"<obsolete_assertion|implementation_defect>\",\n     \"evidence\": { ... }\n   }\n   - \"native\" and \"external\" are TOP-LEVEL string values, exactly one of the two allowed strings each.\n   - \"evidence\" is a SEPARATE nested object holding your supporting detail (e.g. per-case: what requirements.md says, what the test asserted, what the code returned, what you changed). Structure inside \"evidence\" is your call, but keep it factual and specific.\n   - Validate it parses: python3 -m json.tool diagnosis.json (preauthorized).\n4. If you notice unrelated improvement ideas (code quality, test structure, repo hygiene), write them to improvements.md in the project root. Do NOT implement them. If you have none, do not create the file.\n\nHARD CONSTRAINTS\n- Implementation changes are limited to lifecycle.py and test_lifecycle.py. New files diagnosis.json and improvements.md are expected and allowed.\n- Do NOT modify requirements.md or backlog.md, or any other existing file.\n- Do NOT delete any file. Do NOT add dependencies (stdlib only). Do NOT publish anything, do not create artifacts, do not commit or push.\n- Do not act on the pending CEO decision D-7 (transcription provider) \u2014 it is a separate project and out of scope.\n\nREPORT BACK\n- The two classifications and the one-line reason for each.\n- Exact diffs you made (file, before, after).\n- Verbatim test output.\n- The final contents of diagnosis.json and improvements.md (if written)."}, "is_error": false, "tool_denial_kind": null, "timestamp": "2026-09-09T14:47:30.045Z", "result": "[{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata \u2014 never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\\nagentId: abfae99e48ec21b2f (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'abfae99e48ec21b2f', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives \u2014 do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\\nDo not duplicate this agent's work \u2014 avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-private-var-folders-mx-w46p9btx1t17wv9tbsq885qw0000gn-T-richos-owned-wake-native-mmdlv6q8-workspace/fd01ca96-0cfa-4880-bb58-96e8f645855a/tasks/abfae99e48ec21b2f.output\\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool \u2014 it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification.\"}]", "result_truncated": false}], "retry_at": 0, "audit_attempts": 0, "native_tool_requests": {"toolu_01AG2CHQNWSU